<!--
    skin.duotone palette (docs/skin.duotone/DESIGN.md section 2 and "Looks"). Format AARRGGBB.

    THREE LOOKS, ONE SET OF XML (setting duotone.look: empty = Colour, light, dark):
      every look token exists three times here: co_<token> (Colour, the original Duotone), lt_<token> (Light,
      near-white monochrome) and dk_<token> (Dark, near-black monochrome). _src/make_theme.py turns each triple
      into a variable <token> in 1080i/Includes_Theme.xml that returns the right name for the current look.
      Windows ONLY write $VAR[<token>] (or a section variable: $VAR[SectionColor] ...). Never co_/lt_/dk_
      directly, never hex. Lint: python skins/skin.duotone/_src/check_tokens.py
      Add a token = add all three lines and re-run make_theme.py (it refuses an incomplete triple).

    Static colours (the same in every look), the only bare names a window may use:
      white, black, clear (art multipliers, invisible probes) and ground_static (window <backgroundcolor>,
      which takes no $VAR).

    Roles (what a token MEANS, so the monochrome looks can map it):
      sec_*     a section's field (the full-screen colour, panels, OSD slab) and its captions on ink blocks
      chip_*    a section's identity mark on ANOTHER field (search row chips, the settings swatches);
                chiptext_* is the text on it
      ink*      text, rules, frames and blocks on a field; ink_NN = the same at NN % alpha
      scrim     the full-screen dim behind dialogs and menus: always darkens (never write ink_70 for it)
      paper*    text on ink blocks (and on the cobalt field through SectionText); paper_NN = alpha
      tint_* / tintl_*   colordiffuse that makes artwork a one-colour print (Monotone Full / Light)
      print_*   tint for TMDb Helper's black-and-white copy of the big focused art
      dots / dots_art    halftone colour over a field / over a print (white textures)
      track     the settings slider bar
      veil_ghost_* / veil_* / veill_*   field colour at an alpha over a print (clear in Colour)
      bar / bar_fill    the progress marker on posters

    Light and Dark values: visual-designer, DESIGN.md section 9 "Looks: Light and Dark (monochrome)", table 9.2.
    After changing a value re-run make_theme.py + make_textures.py + make_view_previews.py (they bake the
    watched marker, the Dark panel and the Dark previews from these values).
-->
